# Audit trail append-only (rule 248)

Owner design lock 2026-11-20 (evidence needs of A-02, A-05, A-30). Findings: AUD-01, AUD-02, AUD-03, AUD-04.

## Current state (verified 2026-11-20; layer 1 implemented 2026-11-23, not yet released)

Before DMS-SPN4-READY-PILOT-1 R6-B5, `sys_audit_logs` (every `RmeFinancialAuditEvent`) had no model guard and no
trigger, financial event tables were immutable at the model layer only, and `trx_lab_order_status_logs` cascaded on
lab-order delete.

Layer 1 is implemented by migration `2026_11_23_100001_enforce_rule_248_append_only_layer_one`:
- `dms_append_only_guard` triggers refuse UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE on `sys_audit_logs`,
  `trx_lab_order_status_logs` and the five RME `*_events` tables. The function pins `search_path` and is not
  `SECURITY DEFINER`.
- `AuditLog` and `LabOrderStatusLog` refuse update and delete.
- `sys_audit_logs.performed_by` and `trx_lab_order_status_logs.lab_order_id` restrict on delete.
- Owner decision D-Q4-a adds `dms_inventory_ledger_guard` on `trx_inventory_movements`: only a first batch link of the
  movement's own product and branch, and `updated_at`, may change.
- A test that must write such a row (cleanup of committed concurrency fixtures, or an old-shape fixture) uses
  `Tests\Support\Database\AppendOnlyOwnerWrite`, as the table owner. Application code never does.

Until that migration is released, production runs without the triggers. Layers 2 to 5 remain open.

## Locked target

1. Layer 1 (independent of rule 245): model guards refuse update and delete; triggers refuse UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE
   on `sys_audit_logs`, every financial and approval `*_events` table and `trx_lab_order_status_logs`; their foreign
   keys restrict on delete.
2. Layer 2 (with rule 245): the runtime holds SELECT and INSERT only on those tables.
3. Layer 3 (optional, detective): a hash chain verified read-only.
4. Patient merge records the moved ids in an append-only audit row, not only in a mutable case column.
5. An audit written after a rollback asserts transaction level 0.

No agent or operator prunes, edits or truncates these tables; retention is an owner decision executed by the owner role.

## Acceptance criteria

- On PostgreSQL 16, UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE on each listed table fail (trigger now; also SQLSTATE 42501 after
  rule 245).
- Deleting a lab order that has status logs is refused; model update and delete throw; a merge writes one audit row
  listing the moved ids.
